From ab3b85b4ca5098b4b863691ef42fae6d4b956189 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:49:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the teacher choose the main color of the public site
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The navy blue was hardcoded in app.css. A new "Aparência" tab in the admin
lets the teacher pick the main color; the site derives a darker shade (hovers,
footer) and a muted tone of the same hue (body text) in OKLab and overrides
the Tailwind theme variables. Applied to the original navy, the derivation
reproduces the hand-picked shades, and without a chosen color the site keeps
app.css untouched.

Colors whose contrast with the paper background is below 7:1 are rejected,
so the light texts of the dark sections stay legible. The browser theme
color, the favicon and the hero shadows now follow the chosen color too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014fnDHUZWGmsZ82rdp4J4vd
